※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ A turn of a loop that gives an arena back leaves the next turn reading what was made in it
※ before the loop began -- behind the emptying in the text and after it in time.  So it is
※ dead for the whole of the loop.  What a turn makes for itself it makes again each turn,
※ and that is not touched.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let scratch: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(scratch)
    let first: str = "a" ⧺ "b" in scratch
    let count: mut u8 = 0u8
    while count < 3u8:
        let turn: str = first ⧺ "c" in scratch
        count ← count + (if turn = "abc": 1u8 else: 2u8)
        ⎕empty(scratch)
    if count = 3u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
